{"author":{"id":"5698b6d16d951325374257d86a2e673da0e55970c3d21c0f7c6f49018f24e5bf"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1786550941,"nonce":"Zd7zJViUtXpMWNPcB2B5fVvhiZc=","message":"**The headline is now stale; the substance is not.** The title says *\"tabulates six design-enforcement tests and CI runs none of the six\"*. As of the ADR 0028 working tree, §M.7 has **eight** rows and **two of them run**, so both numbers in the title are wrong. Do not read that as progress against *Done when* — it is almost entirely bookkeeping, and the count moved for two different reasons.\n\n**Why eight.** ADR 0028 added two rows for tests that already existed and were simply not tabulated:\n\n- `web/src/index.css.test.ts` — **RUNS** (`npm run test`, `ui` job, `.github/workflows/ci.yml:174`; vitest's `include` is `src/**/*.{test,spec}.{ts,tsx}`). Asserts every first-party utility is declared with `@utility`, and that the reduced-motion guard sweeps `*` rather than naming class names.\n- `web/src/components/ui/Chime.test.tsx` — **RUNS**, same job. Asserts the fūrin's trigger and its `motion-safe:` guard.\n\nNeither is new work done for this ticket. They are gates that existed and that the table did not know about — which is the same documentation defect this ticket describes, pointing the other way.\n\n**Why the six are still six.** Every original row is still unwritten. Re-verified against the tree just now:\n\n- `web/src/design/` holds `.gitkeep`, `theme.ts`, `tokens.css` — no `contrast.test.ts`, no `tokens.test.ts`.\n- `TestNoStateHueInChrome` — still nowhere; `tools/` holds `lintvocab` and `lintreach`, neither of which reads stylesheets or tokens.\n- `web/e2e/` — still one 0-byte `.gitkeep`; still no `playwright`, no `axe`, no e2e script in `web/package.json`.\n- `prefers-reduced-motion` snapshot — still no such test.\n- `TestSlackPaletteUnchanged` — still absent **under that name**, and this row needs a correction the original description got slightly wrong. The hexes are *not* wholly unpinned. `TestTheSlackCardCorpusMatchesItsCheckedInCaptures` (`test/harness/slack_goldens_test.go:50`) byte-compares the rendered corpus against `test/fixtures/slack/*.message.json`, and those captures carry five of the six literals — `#a30200`, `#daa038`, `#dddddd`, `#2eb886`, `#7b1fa2`. `#6b6b6b` (expired) appears in no capture. `TestEachCardStateCarriesItsOwnColourForAHumanToVerify` (`:184`) asserts only that the six are *distinct*, never what they are. So five are pinned incidentally, one is not pinned at all, and nothing pins any of them *to §H.2* — a coordinated edit to `palette.go` and the fixtures passes.\n\n**What changed in the SPEC, and what it is not.** §M.7 now carries a `Status` column marking each row **RUNS** or **UNWRITTEN**, with the evidence for the marking in the row, above a note saying that until this ticket closes an UNWRITTEN row states an intention rather than a gate. §M.6's *\"`TestSlackPaletteUnchanged` pins the six Slack hex values, and a lint rule forbids Slack hex literals in `web/`\"* was false and now says neither exists.\n\n**This is a stopgap, not the fix.** It closes the grep trap the description names — a reader who finds `contrast.test.ts` in the table now reads `UNWRITTEN` in the next column — but it enforces nothing new. *Done when* is unchanged and still governs: every row either names a test CI invokes, or is gone. Keeping this open.\n\n**Suggested retitle:** *\"SPEC §M.7 tabulates eight design-enforcement tests; six are unwritten and marked so\"*.","files":null}]}